structure:
- 1 parent: sends cmd_status to child and waits for ackbyte from child. If received waits and receive data package from child 
- 3 children: 
    detects orientation through high signal at one of its 4 orientation pins (=start bit of CMD_STATUS) -> every communication between child and its parent now takes place through this orientation pin
    receives cmd_status from parent and sends ackByte to parent. 
    Afterwards it transisions into parent role for its children (transmits cmd_status to own children and waits for ack_busy. Saves information about connected children (child_mask) and sends data package to parent (already defined)), 
    combines the received data and sends them back to its own parent 



Difference child_v2 and child_v3 in this prototype: child_v3 additionally indentifies the orientation (pin) of the block 

Transaction:
    1. idle: child waits for CMD_STATUS from parent on PA1
    1. idle: parent releases line
    2. parent: send CMD_STATUS -> reset
    3. parent: releases line

    4. child: receive CMD_STATUS (at one of its 4 orientation pins)
    4.1 v_2_2: every communication between child and its parent now takes place through this orientation pin 
    5. child: send ACK_BUSY upstream on PA1 -> presence
    6. poll children (3x retries): 
          for each retry round:
           for each child i:
               if child already sent data byte -> skip
                send CMD_STATUS
                wait for ACK_BUSY
                if no ACK -> next child
                if ACK received -> wait for DATA_BYTE

    7. child: record child_mask (v2c: computed but not yet sent upstream)
    9. child: send predefined DATA_BYTE upstream on PA1
    9. child: release all lines, return to idle

    10. parent: receives predefined DATA_BYTE
    11: Parent validates SYNC, LEN and CRC
    12: Parent compares payload with expected test payload

Pin assignment:
    PA1 = upstream data line (orientation 0)
    PA3 = upstream port 1 (orientation 1)
    PA4 = upstream port 2 (orientation 2)
    PA5 = upstream port 3 (orientation 3)
    PB0 = downstream child port 0
    PB1 = downstream child port 1
    PA2 = LED